<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Former Irish premier Haughey admitted to hospital.</title>
<headline>Former Irish premier Haughey admitted to hospital.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Former Irish prime minister Charles Haughey was admitted to hospital in Dublin on Monday.</p>
<p>Members of the 71-year-old ex-premier's family said he was undergoing &quot;routine minor tests&quot; and was expected home shortly.</p>
<p>Haughey quit as prime minister and leader of the Fianna Fail political party in 1992 after four terms as head of governments in Dublin.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
